    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will deduce this from Proposition <a href="/tag/BE73FA" data-tag="BE73FA">8.3.1.7</a>. The only nontrivial point is to verify that for any $X \in (\sSet )_{/S}$, the projection $X \times \Delta ^ n \rightarrow X$ is a covariant equivalence. But this map has a section $X \times \{ 0\}  \rightarrow X \times \Delta ^ n$, which is left anodyne and therefore a covariant equivalence (Proposition <a href="/tag/EDA98D" data-tag="EDA98D">2.1.4.9</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
